Dnia Tuesday, 19 of February 2008, pfalcon commit napisa=B3:
> ipkg-utils*: Re-add support for openwrt-style .ipk's.
> * There're two .ipk formats: one with ar top-level wrapping
> (essentially, .deb format, native OE format) and with tar.gz top-level
> wrap, used by OpenWRT and some tiny distros. When I did performance
> optimization work on ipkg-make-index, I just blocked support of
> tar.gz-style ipk's, as it was unclear if those are used in OE at all.
> Now support is readded, with the old code to handle them (i.e. not as
> optimal as ar-style ones).
> * This makes DISTRO=3Dopenwrt-sdk usable for producing compatible
> packages and deploy-feed for them. But there're still some issues to
> resolve before OE can be said to provide seamless support for building
> packages for OpenWRT.

